architecture acquisition-brief-studio
  canonical_name Acquisition Brief Studio
  family surface
  domain Surface / Acquisition review and recipient briefs
  layer application
  semantic_question Which source, checks, verification routes and recommendation belong to the selected opportunity, and what can a reviewer deliver from them?
  purpose A browser workspace over the existing procurement-memory brief contract with independent equipment, property, supplier and civic opportunities, source-bearing memos, eligible route comparisons and recipient exports
  maturity implemented
  source_path ../pages-procurement-memory/site/brief-studio/core.mjs
  source_path ../pages-procurement-memory/site/brief-studio/studio.mjs
  source_path ../pages-procurement-memory/site/brief-studio/composer.mjs
  source_path ../pages-procurement-memory/site/brief-studio/index.html
  source_path ../pages-procurement-memory/site/brief-studio/vendor/tiptap-3.32.0/provenance.json
  source_path ../pages-procurement-memory/tests/brief-studio.test.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/brief-studio-browser.mjs
  node_types Opportunity, ProofNeed, VerificationRoute, EditorialSnapshot, ReviewerMemo, RecipientBrief
  internal_calculus eligible proof-kind coverage, exact integer-cent cost and shared-provider travel group pricing, bounded route subset optimization and explicit route exclusion
  internal_calculus version-two editorial migration preserves legacy values once and retains recommendation, recipient, memo, budget, comparison mode and section choices per opportunity
  internal_calculus browser saves compare the expected workspace revision in one IndexedDB write transaction; edits arriving during an in-flight save remain dirty and are saved separately
  internal_calculus Tiptap documents are validated against bounded node and mark types before persistence and HTML or Markdown export; a failed optional editor leaves the plain text field and recoverable draft
  invariant unfinished quote edits block case or domain changes until saved or cancelled; invalid candidate routes never mutate the opportunity; failed saved-workspace reads preserve unsaved edits and current identity
  invariant excluded routes remain available for comparison but never appear as selected routes in the typed proposal
  invariant proposed coverage and locally reviewed check status are distinct; quoted-ready mode requires a recorded reference without claiming provider verification
  invariant native Economy retains approval and dispatch authority; the browser downloads a proposal and performs no provider or native admission request
  witness ../pages-procurement-memory/tests/brief-studio.test.mjs passes 20 tests for route eligibility, exact costs, exclusion, source preservation, safe note export, independent records and versioned migration
  witness packs/no-simulation/product-maturity-20261015/brief/local/verification.json records 55 fresh-Chrome checks including formatted notes, quote edits, imports, independent settings, revision conflicts, failure recovery and phone views
  witness packs/no-simulation/product-maturity-20261015/brief/live/verification.json repeats the 55-check journey on the published branch preview with no browser exceptions or remote writes
  witness packs/no-simulation/product-maturity-20261015/brief/deployment.json names preview deployment e8875e2b-6dc2-49cf-8f59-3ab119d8c9b6 and unchanged Work Samples production deployment
  forbidden_inference a usable browser brief or complete proposed coverage -> a shared account workspace, organization authority, verified supplier evidence, native approval or booking
  forbidden_inference the preview deployment -> a new GitHub commit, changed GitHub Pages, or completion of all thirty demo programs
  known_gap source is owned by the sibling pages-procurement-memory checkout; GitHub Pages remains on its committed version and the preview origin has separate browser storage
  known_gap account and organization persistence, review handoff admission, collaborative editing, full workspace backup and Google Stitch design generation remain open
